T*
(icon gallery . In the past, the work to do this was a bit tedious. First, I?d find the app in) Tj
T*
(the ?Applications? folder \(or elsewhere on the Mac\), right click and choose ?Get Info?:) Tj
T*
(Right-click the app icon in the Get Info pane and choose ?Copy?: Open the Preview app and go) Tj
T*
(?File -> New from Clipboard?: This gets me the app icon file with a variety of sizes \(the) Tj
T*
(1024-pixel version is the one I want\). From here, I go ?File -> Export??, choose ?PNG?, and) Tj
T*
(name the file as the app name, lowercased, hyphenated ? e.g. ?app-store.png? \(I do this for) Tj
T*
(automation purposes not relevant here\). Doing that for every Apple-supplied app in the OS can) Tj
T*
(get tiring. It?s often upwards of 75+ icons. ?This seems like the perfect task for an LLM,? I) Tj
T*
(thought. So I hastily wrote a prompt to see if it could do it. And it did ? sort of, after a) Tj
